WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.987
Meet Hoard. Find and share the resources you already have, without
moving or renaming your files.

00:00:06.987 --> 00:00:18.434
Name your node and review its sharing address. Saved settings apply
after a restart. This demonstration uses a local address, reachable only
from this machine.

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:27.114
Add a folder from the machine running Hoard. Auto-detect recognizes Git
projects, model folders, and Hugging Face caches.

00:00:27.114 --> 00:00:35.022
Choose Add and Scan. Hoard indexes your resources in place, while your
original files stay untouched.

00:00:35.022 --> 00:00:43.329
Add another folder to bring your collection together. These small
demonstration models show the same workflow you can use with your own
collection.

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:52.658
Projects and models share one searchable index. Select a row to see its
details in the inspector. Open it when you want to explore further.

00:00:52.658 --> 00:01:01.049
Find a project by its name, the text in its read me, or its file paths.
A Git project does not need to contain a model.

00:01:01.049 --> 00:01:08.445
Read the project's documentation before downloading it. Follow links to
related guides, and check the selected revision.

00:01:08.445 --> 00:01:15.946
Browse the files and preview their content. Press Escape to return to
the file list without losing your place.

00:01:15.946 --> 00:01:25.364
Copy the clone command and use Git as usual. Hoard serves the repository
directly, so its source files and documentation travel together.

00:01:25.364 --> 00:01:39.169
To share with other machines, configure a reachable network address and
check that it works from another computer. Keep adding folders as your
collection grows. Find it, review it, and share it with Hoard.
